# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated files: written by a program, never versioned
#
# Two sets, from three writers. matugen renders the first from the current
# wallpaper, so they change every time the background does; `desktop-opacity`
# and `desktop-font` write the second from the settings window. What is
# versioned is the template or the config that READS them, never the result.
#
# THESE RULES CANNOT MATCH ANYTHING TODAY, and that is not a reason to drop
# them. install.sh stows with --no-folding, which creates real directories and
# links file by file, so a program writing a new file into ~/.config lands in
# ~/.config and not in this repository -- verified: none of the paths below
# exists here, while every one of them exists under ~. The rules are the net
# for the day somebody stows WITHOUT --no-folding, where the whole directory
# is linked and every one of these would appear as an untracked file inside
# the repo. An earlier version of this comment said that showing up as
# "modified" after a stow was expected; with --no-folding it is not, and if it
# ever happens something is wrong rather than normal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# From the wallpaper, by matugen.
kitty/.config/kitty/colors.conf
hypr/.config/hypr/colors.lua
gtk/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css
gtk/.config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css
ranger/.config/ranger/accent
quickshell/.config/quickshell/colors.json

# From the settings window, by desktop-opacity and desktop-font. The configs
# that include them -- kitty.conf and userChrome.css -- are versioned; these
# are not.
kitty/.config/kitty/opacity.conf
kitty/.config/kitty/font.conf

# Zen writes outside .config: its chrome/ only counts inside the profile,
# ~/.zen/rice. The versioned part is userChrome.css (zen/.zen/rice/chrome/),
# which imports both of these.
zen/.zen/rice/chrome/colors.css
zen/.zen/rice/chrome/opacity.css

# zathura and fastfetch are generated WHOLE from a template: they have no stow
# package of their own. See matugen/.config/matugen/config.toml.
#
# ~/.config/qt6ct/colors/matugen.conf is generated too, but there is nothing to
# ignore: qt6ct has no stow package either. Its config is a seed (seeds/), so
# the whole directory is the machine's and matugen writes outside the repo.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
openrgb/.config/OpenRGB/logs/
openrgb/.config/OpenRGB/plugins/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Executables that live in bin/ but are not this repo's to ship
#
# Two different cases, both landing in ~/.local/bin and neither belonging in
# git. cship is COMPILED: its configuration is versioned under shell/ and the
# binary is built, not stored. claude is INSTALLED BY ITS OWN TOOL -- what is
# at that path is a symlink into ~/.local/share/claude/versions/, so tracking
# it would version a pointer at one machine's install. Its icon
# (icons/.local/share/icons/claude.png) IS tracked, because that one really is
# an asset the desktop entry needs and the application does not provide.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
bin/.local/bin/cship
bin/.local/bin/claude

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# General junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.bak
*.old
*~
.cache/

# Links created by `systemctl --user enable`. They are regenerated, not
# versioned: install.sh does it.
systemd/.config/systemd/user/*.target.wants/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local Hyprland pieces
#
# monitors.lua and tweaks.lua are written by the `hypr-monitor` and
# `hypr-tweak` scripts from the settings window; local.lua is hand-written and
# holds whatever belongs to one machine or one person (keyboard layout, extra
# binds, window rules). None of them may be versioned: the repo is shared with
# another machine and another layout, and a tracked personal file turns every
# pull over there into a conflict. hyprland.lua loads all three with pcall, so
# not having them is the normal case.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
hypr/.config/hypr/monitors.lua
hypr/.config/hypr/tweaks.lua
hypr/.config/hypr/local.lua
